  "caveats": [
    "Test errors of one skill are correlated across origins, so the effective sample is much smaller than the raw count. The skill bootstrap respects this; the raw pair count does not.",
    "The pooled model has ~25 eligible skills and at most ~47 training origins. Training rows from consecutive origins overlap heavily, so the data is small and highly correlated.",
    "ai_level is nearly a time index (it rises through the whole period). The model can memorise time with it; trees cannot extrapolate beyond the range seen in training.",
    "ai_exposure and e_s (exposure.csv) are not time-cut: the same 2026-06 value is used at every origin. They are constant per skill, so they act as skill identifiers.",
    "The first EARLY origins have too few training rows for a model; they use naive3. early_mature (2022-11..2023-10) is the fair EARLY comparison.",
    "Permutation importance is computed on the training set (in-sample), as specified.",
    "The last target month (2026-10) comes from an HN thread that was still open when fetched.",
    "Production forecasting is unchanged by this experiment; a promote verdict needs review."
